course: dictionary
lesson: 3931
title: Frustrating: when you cannot change something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Frustrating describes something that makes you feel cross and upset because you cannot do or change it. «Losing your homework again is so frustrating.» You cannot change the fact that it is lost, so you feel cross.
explain: Frustrating is the «-ing» form of the verb frustrate. Look at the clues around the word. «When practice is frustrating, break the skill into small steps and practise one at a time.» The small steps tell you that frustrating feels like something hard that is stuck.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Getting better at anything takes practice, and practice can be frustrating.» If you put "makes me cross because I can't do it yet" in place of frustrating, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Frustrating means making you feel cross and upset because you cannot do or change something.
fact: Frustrating is an adjective, so it describes a thing: a frustrating day, or a frustrating puzzle.
fact: Its comparison forms are more frustrating and most frustrating.
fact: Frustrating is the «-ing» form of the verb frustrate.
fact: Useful phrases are «so frustrating», «it's frustrating when...» and «a frustrating day».
exercise: «Losing your homework is so frustrating.» What does frustrating mean? | *Makes you feel cross and upset because you cannot do or change it | Makes you feel happy and proud | Makes you feel very sleepy | Makes you feel hungry
exercise: Frustrate is a verb. Which word is its «-ing» form? | Frustrate | Frustration | *Frustrating
exercise: «When practice is frustrating, what should you do?» | *Break the skill into small steps and practise one at a time | Throw your book across the room | Sit and stare at the wall | Give up at once
test: Which form is correct for comparing something that is the strongest kind of frustrating? | frustratingest | *most frustrating | frustrating more | more frustrating
test: Which sentence uses frustrating correctly? | *It's frustrating when my phone battery dies in the middle of a game. | Frustrating the cake was eaten by the dog. | The frustrating sang a happy song in the park.
exam: Which word best fits? «Mia tried the puzzle ten times and could not solve it; it was so ___.» | *Frustrating | Relaxing | Funny | Quiet
